        <button class="btn cmd danger" id="ca-drop" data-icon="trash"
                title="Take the stored authority away. The server's certificate then has to be signed by one this machine already trusts.">Take it away</button>
        <input type="file" id="ca-input" accept=".pem,.crt,.cer,.txt" hidden>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="card full">
      <h2>The groups, and what each one may do</h2>
      <p class="note">Press <b>Find the groups</b> and pick them out of the directory rather
        than typing a distinguished name by hand — that is how a role ends up pointing at a
        group that does not exist, and nobody finds out until the first person cannot sign
        in.</p>
      <div class="btnrow admin-only">
        <button class="btn cmd primary" id="dir-find" data-icon="search"
                title="Ask the directory what groups there are. Nothing is changed; it only reads.">Find the groups</button>
