  <div class="ctl-pane" id="pane-dir2" hidden>
    <div class="ctl-head">
      <h2 class="ctl-title">A second directory</h2>
      <p class="ctl-lede">For the site that signs its administrators in against one domain
        while the people in its ISE logs live in another. When a name is not in the first
        directory, this one is asked — and that is the whole of what it is for.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="card full">
      <p class="note"><b>Nobody ever signs in against this one.</b> No role comes from its
        groups, no account is made from it, and it is never consulted when somebody types a
        password into this dashboard. It answers one question: who is this name. Like the
        first, it is only ever read — there is no write to a directory anywhere in this
        program.</p>
